<title>USA: Schweitzer-Mauduit joins SmallCap index.</title>
<headline>Schweitzer-Mauduit joins SmallCap index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said on Tuesday that it will replace Production Operators Corp in the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index with Schweitzer-Mauduit International Inc after Friday, June 13, 1997.</p>
<p>Production Operators is being acquired by Camco International Inc in a stock merger and the shareholder votes will take place on that date.</p>
<p>Schweitzer-Mauduit is the world's largest manufacturer of fine papers used by the tobacco industry, Standard &amp; Poor's said.</p>
</text>
